ial once this handler is reached."}],"policyAssessment":{"status":"satisfied","explanation":"The supplied policy says only a space administrator may remove another member. The service rejects a non-self request unless the caller membership is ADMIN, and all three visible database backends repeat that requirement."}},{"questionId":"delete-space-member-visible-paths","behavior":{"disposition":"conditional","explanation":"Yes. The administrator-removal and self-removal paths differ at the role guard: deleting a different member requires the caller's membership to be ADMIN, while deleting oneself bypasses that administrator check. Both paths then delete the resolved target membership and remain subject to common validity and integrity checks, notably that deleting an active administrator cannot leave the space without an active administrator."},"branches":[{"id":"administrator-different-member","condition":"The authenticated caller targets a different active member in the selected space and callerMembership.Role is ADMIN.","disposition":"conditional","explanation":"Because the target differs from the current user, the service executes requireSpaceAdministrator. An ADMIN caller passes and the store is asked to delete the target membership identified by targetMembership.SpaceID and targetMembership.UserID. The database backends recheck that a non-self actor is an active administrator. Deletion can still fail if the target is absent or if removing the target would remove the last active administrator; otherwise the active membership row is deleted.","evidenceIds":["ev-3f913436015dacb5a046","ev-2ffb20e72c767923a83d","ev-7a80e5045e5259c2eebb","ev-ef3f9a6f661d54b87eae","ev-e29fb091e04b74dd359a","ev-21f5cf9514ab3804eac2","ev-4613bf5cc02521f91db5"]},{"id":"self-removal","condition":"The target user resolved from request.name has the same ID as the authenticated current user.","disposition":"conditional","explanation":"The isSelf comparison is true, so the service does not invok